# Rank 1192 / CVE-2023-42276: hutool's JSONArray.add(int, Object) pads the
# backing list up to a caller-supplied index before placing the element
# (GHSA-rxgf-r843-g53h, issue#3286@Github). When index is at or past the
# current size, the vulnerable form loops `while (index != this.size())
# this.add(JSONNull.NULL);`, appending one JSONNull per step with no upper
# bound on index -- a single call with a large index drives the loop until
# the JVM runs out of heap. hutool-core's ListUtil.setOrPadding has the
# identical padding loop and the same fix; the advisory names both
# artifacts, and the fix (9ba8f9ca5) lands the same two-line guard in both.
# The first tagged release carrying the fix is 5.8.22.
#
# The weakness is inside the library, so the application's call is correct
# code -- there is no application-side pattern that separates a vulnerable
# pin from a fixed one -- and the report that belongs to this CVE is the
# dependency finding: a Maven pin of either artifact below 5.8.22. The
# advisory's own CWE-120 label describes a memory-safety violation that this
# loop is not; the class is unbounded resource consumption, so the row
# carries CWE-400.

test "rank1192: a hutool-json pin below the first index-bounded release is a dependency finding"
  lang java
  file src/main/java/example/App.java
  code
  ```
  package example;

  import cn.hutool.json.JSONArray;

  public class App {
      public void place(JSONArray array, int index, Object value) {
          array.add(index, value);
      }
  }
  ```
  file pom.xml
  code
  ```
  <project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0">
    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>
    <groupId>example</groupId>
    <artifactId>app</artifactId>
    <version>1.0.0</version>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency>
        <groupId>cn.hutool</groupId>
        <artifactId>hutool-json</artifactId>
        <version>5.8.21</version>
      </dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </project>
  ```
  expect VYQL-SCA-001
  expect_evidence VYQL-SCA-001 CVE-2023-42276

